{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-23 requires the driver, before cancelling for no-show, to have sent at least one in-app chat message AND to have placed at least one in-app call, both before trip_record.cancelled_at. The record shows the call limb only — a single in-app call at 11:14:20 that was not answered and rang 20 s (EV-TRIP-05065) — and no chat message from the driver at all: the chat log's one and only entry is the rider's own message at 11:06:00, and the platform's own derived contact_before_cancel block returns message_count 0, complete false and obligation_met false (EV-CHAT-05065). I rely on EV-CHAT-05065 as impaired evidence: TRUNCATED_LOG, weight_multiplier 0.6, 1 of 3 entries exported with nothing after 11:06:00. On the record as it stands the message limb of the contact obligation fails, and POL-NS-23 is express that the fee is then voided 'with no driver compensation' — so the driver cannot recover the 5.00 under POL-NS-22 even though he cancelled 380 s after arriving.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05065", "EV-CHAT-05065"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23", "POL-NS-22", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.contact_before_cancel.obligation_met",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's claim says he 'sent message and called', but the trip record's own event log shows what actually happened at that pickup: a platform push notification at 11:11:54 ('Your driver has arrived') and one in-app call at 11:14:20 that was not answered (EV-TRIP-05065). A system push is not an in-app chat message, and an unanswered call is not a message; POL-NS-23 requires both limbs, each before the cancellation, and nothing in this record supplies the message limb. The chat log I rely on for that is impaired — TRUNCATED_LOG, weight_multiplier 0.6 (EV-CHAT-05065).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05065", "EV-CHAT-05065"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.in_app_calls",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "If the judge reads the truncated chat export as leaving the message limb unproved rather than disproved, the rider still wins the money point: whether the driver messaged before cancelling is a fact POL-NS-23 needs, and the only evidence that would carry it is impaired — the export holds 1 entry against trip_record.chat_message_count of 3 and covers nothing after 11:06:00, so the arrival and the whole waiting window are absent (EV-CHAT-05065, weight_multiplier 0.6, TRUNCATED_LOG; EV-TRIP-05065). POL-GEN-26 names this very fact ('whether the driver messaged and called before cancelling') and requires escalation. ESCALATE is terminal, issues no monetary outcome and holds the amount, so the 5.00 already refunded to the rider is not restored to the driver and no fee is collected from the rider. POL-NS-26 expressly subjects even a final no-show ruling to POL-GEN-26.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05065", "EV-TRIP-05065"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-26", "POL-NS-26", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.contact_before_cancel.reason",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "I do not contest the wait, and I say so plainly: POL-NS-21's free wait runs 300 s from the driver's arrival, the record puts arrival at 11:11:50 and cancellation at 11:18:10 — 380 s — and the GPS trace corroborates the arrival, the nearest fix sitting 2.05 m from the pickup at 11:12:30 with 5.0 m reported accuracy, well inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius (EV-GPS-05065; EV-TRIP-05065). That discharges POL-NS-21 and it does nothing for POL-NS-23, which is a separate and cumulative contact obligation the driver must also satisfy before he may cancel for no-show.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05065", "EV-GPS-05065"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21", "POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "derived.v7.arrival_check.nearest_fix",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The filer here is the driver (dispute.filed_by = DRIVER) and the disputed 5.00 is already off the rider: the ledger records payment_status REFUNDED with refund_issued_sgd 5.00 against total_charged 5.00 (EV-FARE-05065), and the trip record records the fee_reversed event at 13:59:10 — 5.00 refunded to the rider and withheld from the driver (EV-TRIP-05065). What the driver seeks is restoration of that 5.00 to himself. POL-GEN-03 defines FULL_REFUND against the filing party, so on a driver's filing FULL_REFUND would run to the driver; it is not the rider's remedy and the rider does not ask for it. The rider's entitlement is that the disputed charge is not collected, which is exactly what the present state already achieves: NO_ACTION — the filing party's claim not supported, both amount fields null and no driver compensation.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05065", "EV-TRIP-05065"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.derived.money.refund_already_issued_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No POL-NS-25 repeat-no-show referral is available on this profile. EV-RPROF-05065 carries no no_show_cancellations_30d counter at all, and POL-NS-25 applies only where that counter is present, so the flag cannot be computed and must not be manufactured from the record. The profile's no_show_disputes_30d is a different field, is CONTEXT ONLY under POL-GEN-01, and may not be used to qualify or decide this trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-05065"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-25", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
